# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local
.vercel
.env
.env.local
backend/.data

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
agent/.data

# Firebase service-account keys — the console downloads these as a JSON file
# with a name like my-project-firebase-adminsdk-ab12c-3d4e5f6a7b.json.
# Copy the three fields you need into .env.local instead of committing it.
*firebase-adminsdk*.json
serviceAccountKey.json

# Source questionnaire forms. Kept locally to transcribe wording from, but
# they are published third-party documents rather than part of this codebase —
# instruments.js carries the wording, its licence and its citation.
*.pdf

.vercel

# Secrets only. .env.example and .env.production are committed on purpose —
# the examples document what each module needs, and .env.production carries
# the public build config (VITE_API_URL, VITE_AGENT_URL) that the Vercel build
# reads. Without these negations a bare `.env*` swallows both, and the day one
# is re-added it disappears instead.
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.production

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The repository root is an allowlist.
#
# Nineteen AI assistants and editors have each dropped a config directory
# beside the app — .cursor, .windsurf, .kiro, .roo, .trae and the rest.
# Enumerating them was a losing game: the list was already nineteen long
# and the twentieth tool arrives next week, unlisted and committed.
#
# So the root ignores everything and names the exceptions. Five source
# modules, three files, and the GitHub directory. Anything else that
# appears up here is somebody's tool, and it stays out on its own.
#
# `/*` matches only root-level entries, so nothing inside the modules is
# affected — the .env.example negations further up still work, and every
# node_modules and dist is still caught by its own rule.
#
# To add a real root file later, negate it here. That is the cost of the
# allowlist and the whole reason it is written down.
/*

!/admin/
!/agent/
!/backend/
!/frontend/
!/scripts/

!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/package.json

# Allowed as a directory, empty in practice. It holds only a prompt
# library today, which the rule below ignores — but .github is also where
# workflows, issue templates and CODEOWNERS belong, and ignoring it
# outright would swallow the first workflow anybody adds, without a word.
!/.github/
.github/prompts/
